{
  // Adeptsworn public website — https://adeptsworn.com
  //
  // THIS WORKER NOW DOES THREE JOBS. They were built at different times and
  // they must not tread on each other. src/router.js is the front door and
  // says which is which; read that file first.
  //
  //   1. Discord sign-in        /auth/*        src/index.js   (8 Sept)
  //   2. The game's server list /api/servers   src/index.js   (10 Sept)
  //   3. The website and its    /              src/site.js    (12 Sept)
  //      editor                 /admin-api/*
  //
  // "name" MUST match the existing Cloudflare Worker exactly. Change it and
  //   wrangler builds a NEW Worker under the new name and leaves the domain
  //   pointing at the old one. It is an identity, not a label.
  // "compatibility_date" pins the Cloudflare runtime behaviour to how it
  //   worked on this date, so a future change on their end cannot silently
  //   alter how the site is served. Leave it alone unless you have a reason.
  // "main" USED to be ./src/index.js and is now ./src/router.js. index.js is
  //   unchanged and still does everything it did; the router just decides
  //   what reaches it. That was the safest way to add a third job: the code
  //   that already works was not opened.
  //
  // ------------------------------------------------------------------
  //  assets.run_worker_first — READ THIS BEFORE CHANGING IT
  // ------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Cloudflare serves a matching FILE before it runs any code. index.html is
  // still sitting in this folder, so without this line "/" would be served
  // from that file and the Worker would never build the page. The failure
  // would be silent: the site would simply stop updating, with no error
  // anywhere, looking exactly like a deploy that did nothing.
  //
  // index.html is deliberately still published. If this line is ever removed
  // or stops working, the site falls back to the hand-written page of
  // 10 September rather than to nothing at all.
  //
  // /auth/* and /api/servers are NOT listed here and do not need to be —
  // there are no files at those addresses, so they reach the Worker anyway.
  // That is how they have always worked and this changes nothing for them.
  //
  // ------------------------------------------------------------------
  //  WHY THE CLIENT ID IS IN THIS FILE AND THE SECRETS ARE NOT
  // ------------------------------------------------------------------
  // The Discord Client ID is PUBLIC BY DESIGN. It travels in the address bar
  // of every person who signs in, so putting it in a public repo gives away
  // nothing that was not already on show. DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET,
  // SESSION_SECRET, LOBBY_SECRET and ADMIN_PASSWORD are Cloudflare secrets
  // and must never appear here.
  //
  // ------------------------------------------------------------------
  //  THE TWO KV STORES ARE NOT INTERCHANGEABLE
  // ------------------------------------------------------------------
  // LOBBY holds the game's server list. SITE holds the website's words and
  // colours. They are separate on purpose: a website edit can never reach
  // the game's data, and the game can never overwrite the site.

  "name": "wispy-brook-7be4",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-06",
  "main": "./src/router.js",

  "vars": {
    "DISCORD_CLIENT_ID": "1546109338169639013"
  },

  "kv_namespaces": [
    {
      "binding": "LOBBY",
      "id": "e668e5a9663f425a8fc01a8289ff536d"
    },
    {
      "binding": "SITE",
      "id": "28e125a7ca36482d8915781959ca2ce2"
    }
  ],

  "assets": {
    "directory": "./",
    "binding": "ASSETS",
    "run_worker_first": ["/", "/index.html", "/admin-api/*", "/media/*"]
  },

  "observability": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
